{"name":"Lilac Smoke","hex":"#b6a3a0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lilac","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large shrub of the genus Syringa, especially Syringa vulgaris, bearing white, pale-pink, or purple flowers.","A flower of the lilac shrub."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a pale purple colour.","Of a cat or its fur: having a pale brown colour, lighter than chocolate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lilac"},{"term":"smoke","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The visible vapor/vapour, gases, and fine particles given off by burning or smoldering material.","A cigarette."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To inhale and exhale the smoke from a burning cigarette or cigar, burning material in a pipe, etc.","To inhale and exhale tobacco smoke."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smoke"}],"entries":[{"title":"Syringa","blocks":[{"text":"Syringa is a genus of 12 currently recognized species of flowering woody plants in the olive family known colloquially as lilacs. They are native to woodland and scrub from southeastern Europe to eastern Asia, and widely and commonly cultivated in temperate areas elsewhere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Stockholm-lilac.jpg/330px-Stockholm-lilac.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syringa","wikidata":"Q157449"},{"title":"Smoke","blocks":[{"text":"Smoke is an aerosol emitted when a material undergoes combustion or pyrolysis, together with the quantity of air that is entrained or otherwise mixed into the mass. It is commonly an unwanted by-product of fires, but may also be used for pest control (fumigation), communication, defensive and offensive capabilities in the military, cooking, or smoking. It is used in rituals where incense, sage, or resin is burned to produce a smell for spiritual or magical purposes. It can also be a flavoring agent and preservative."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Ognisko_ubt_0126.jpeg/330px-Ognisko_ubt_0126.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smoke","wikidata":"Q130768"},{"title":"Lilac (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lilac is a light shade of purple or violet representing the average color of most lilac flowers. The colors of some lilac flowers may be equivalent to the colors shown below as pale lilac, rich lilac, or deep lilac. However, there are other lilac flowers that are colored red-violet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Stockholm-lilac.jpg/330px-Stockholm-lilac.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lilac_(color)","wikidata":"Q12894641"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Lilac_Bush.jpg/500px-Lilac_Bush.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Lilac_Bush.jpg/1280px-Lilac_Bush.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Lilac_Bush.jpg/500px-Lilac_Bush.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Purple lilac bush","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALilac_Bush.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Lilac_buds.jpg/500px-Lilac_buds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Lilac_buds.jpg/500px-Lilac_buds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dormant lilac buds","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALilac_buds.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Lilac.